From 15ec8352ae34c4fc1990536d27c52a6c725a4361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shivam Rawat <shivam.rawat@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:01:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: Fix stale rpmh votes after suspend

a6xx_rpmh_stop() bails out precisely when GMU_STATUS_FW_START is set --
that is, whenever the GMU firmware was actually started and the RPMh
sleep sequence therefore needs to run. Conversely it runs the sequence
only when the bit was already clear and there is nothing to stop.

The condition is inverted. Note the neighbouring a6xx_rpmh_start() uses
the negated form for GMU_STATUS_PDC_SLEEP; restore the symmetry.

Consequence is that the GPU RSC is never told to sleep on the way down,
leaving RPMh votes behind after GPU suspend and holding SoC power
resources up.

Backported for 7.2 from Rob Clark's drm-msm-next-2026-08-01 pull request
for v7.3 (shortlog: "drm/msm/a6xx: Fix stale rpmh votes after suspend").
Verified identical in 7.1 and 7.2, i.e. this is long-standing rather than
a 7.2 regression. The upstream commit message and SHA were unavailable --
the tag was obtained as a source snapshot without git history -- so this
text is reconstructed; only the one-character code change is upstream's.

Signed-off-by: Shivam Rawat <shivam.rawat@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 2e5d7b53a..51010d46a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -642,7 +642,7 @@ static void a6xx_rpmh_stop(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
 		return;
 
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu))
